  "settled_contract": [
    "A Step Run has exactly one immediate Workflow Run or containing Step Run in Header.Container.",
    "An Action Run launched by a Step Run names that Step Run as its Header.Container.",
    "The Container Property is the sole stored parentage; retain formal IS_CONTAINED_BY/CONTAINS views without automatic inverse permission."
  ],
  "finding": "R2749 declares Execution, while R2750–R2752 declare three distinct narrower kinds; inspected sources do not declare a shared Run kind, any Run.Header group, or a Run-identity reference Format. Atom.Header and its Atom-ID format cannot automatically govern non-Atom Executions. Step/Action Draft previews state the settled local constraints but depend on explicit Header group and Property declarations and their value Format before adoption.",
  "question": "What value identifies a Workflow Run or Step Run in Header.Container: an existing Run identity/reference Format, or a newly specified Run reference Format?",
  "gate": "Define only necessary Run Header group/Container Property declarations after the value Format and common owner are resolved; no global Node header, invented Workflow Run root, additional Action Run universal cardinality, or stored Relation fact. Preserve source Draft metadata and all unrelated Run behavior.",
  "limits": "Source-only previews; no native source, code, tests, actual Workflow, Workbench or Git mutation."
}
